# Eval-loop agent

When working on `harness/agent/`, `LOOP.md`, recipes, or prompt-eval flow:

- Read `LOOP.md` before implementing. Sessions A–E are listed there.
- Mine problems from shift JSON (`events` + `baseline`) only. Do not invent guard personas or synthetic replies.
- Photos in the bundle are `[photo]` placeholders, not inspectable duplicates.
- Deterministic scorers own PASS/FAIL. Diagnostician and patcher never flip a gate.
- Live control is same-model original prompt, not historical baseline.
- Improvement on static JSON is process-spec lift (`variant_spec_rate > control_spec_rate`) on frozen turns, plus preserve + holdout. Do not score later historical guard replies as outcomes.
- One prompt file per iteration. Holdout safety (`55252` / catalog holdout) must not fail before keep.
- Raise or implement `SessionTodo`; do not silently fake a stage.
